      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "Find the scale factor of the transformation represented by the rotation-scaling matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "The scale factor $r$ of the rotation-scaling matrix $[\\begin{aligned}a & -b \\\\ b & a\\end{aligned}]$ can be found using the formula \n\n$$\nr=\\sqrt{det(A)}=\\sqrt{{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\sqrt{det(A)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+(2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{20} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
